<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore von Neuhoff</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1694–1756</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Theodore of Corsica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore von Neuhoff was a Westphalian adventurer who was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a> in April 1736 by islanders in revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. He landed with arms and money obtained abroad, set up a court, created knighthoods and minted coins, but left the island within eight months to seek help and never re-established his rule. He later spent years in a debtors' prison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and died there in poverty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-von-neuhoff.jpg" alt="Theodore von Neuhoff" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jastiriare · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Theodore_of_Corsica.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
